$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=flsqrt2  LOC_AFTER=?

* The integer square root of a nonnegative real is a nonnegative integer whose square is at most the argument, and the argument is below the square of its successor.

s1::simpl |- ( ( A e. RR /\ 0 <_ A ) -> A e. RR )
s2::simpr |- ( ( A e. RR /\ 0 <_ A ) -> 0 <_ A )
